// [id:planet-red] [tag:mcq-level-1] [tag:mcq-time-20]
::Red planet::Which planet is called the red planet?{
	=Mars#Iron oxide colours its soil.
	~Venus#Venus is covered in yellowish clouds.
	~Jupiter
	####Mars owes its colour to rust.
}

::Moons::Which planets have moons?{
	~%50%Earth
	~%50%Mars
	~%-100%Venus#Venus has no moon.
}

::Sun::The Sun is a star.{TRUE#Wrong, it is a star.#Right.}

::Pluto::Pluto is still a planet.{F}

$CATEGORY: $course$/top/Default for Demo/Symbols

::Escapes::[markdown]In GIFT, which character writes \= literally?{
	=A backslash \ before it
	~A colon \: after it
}

::Gap::Light from the Sun reaches us in about {=8 minutes ~8 seconds ~8 hours}, not instantly.

::Speed::How fast is light, in km/s?{#300000:1000}

::Essay::Describe a comet.{}

::Pairs::Match the planets.{=Mars -> red =Venus -> yellow}

::Short::Name the closest star.{=Sun =the Sun}

